</surname><given-names>FX</given-names></name><name><surname>Lotan</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>N-(4-hydroxyphenyl)retinamide-induced apoptosis triggered by reactive oxygen species is mediated by activation of MAPKs in head and neck squamous carcinoma cells</article-title><source>Oncogene</source><year>2006</year><volume>25</volume><fpage>2785</fpage><lpage>2794</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16407847</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B17"><label>17</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sun</surname><given-names>SY</given-names></name><name><surname>Li</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Yue</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Lippman</surname><given-names>SM</given-names></name><name><surname>Hong</surname><given-names>WK</given-names></name><name><surname>Lotan</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Mediation of N-(4-hydoxyphenyl)retinamide-induced apoptosis in human cancer cells by different mechanisms</article-title><source>Cancer Res</source><year>1999</year><volume>59</volume><fpage>2493</fpage><lpage>2498</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10344763</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B18"><label>18</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Zou</surname><given-names>CP</given-names></name><name><surname>Kurie</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Lotan</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Zou</surname><given-names>CC</given-names></name><name><surname>Hong</surname><given-names>WK</given-names></name><name><surname>Lotan</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Higher potency of N-(4-hydroxyphenyl)retinamide than all-trans-retinoic acid in induction of apoptosis in non-small cell lung cancer cell lines</article-